s: eth1 (172.20.1.1/24, toward node2) and eth2 (172.20.2.1/24, toward node3), with IPv4 forwarding enabled globally and per-interface. Configured node2's enp8s0 as 172.20.1.2/24 and node3's enp8s0 as 172.20.2.2/24 via NetworkManager static profiles, each with a static route to the other's segment via node1. Verified node2<->node3 reachability through node1. Persisted node1's config via /etc/network/interfaces.d/60-antrieb-segments (auto-applied by SONiC's networking service, sourced from the stock interfaces template) and /etc/sysctl.d/99-antrieb.conf (applied at boot by systemd-sysctl). Restarted node1 with a native `reboot`, confirmed a changed boot_id after it came back (SONiC boot took ~4 minutes), confirmed eth1/eth2 addresses and forwarding sysctls returned automatically without any post-boot intervention, and re-verified node2<->node3 ping succeeded with 0% loss in both directions. node2 and node3 were not restarted (task scoped the restart to node1 only; they were never disrupted so no restart evidence applies to them).\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed topology and interfaces on node1/node2/node3 (ip addr, ip route, /etc/hosts, CLUSTER_HOSTS)\",\"Inspected SONiC's interfaces-config.sh and interfaces.j2 template to determine a persistence-safe config location\",\"Cleaned up node1's docker0 class-E address per SONiC gotchas and assigned eth1/eth2 addresses\",\"Enabled net.ipv4.ip_forward and per-interface forwarding on node1 (eth1, eth2)\",\"Wrote /etc/network/interfaces.d/60-antrieb-segments and /etc/sysctl.d/99-antrieb.conf on node1 for boot-time persistence\",\"Reconfigured node2 and node3's second NIC (enp8s0) to static IPs via nmcli, with static routes to each other's segment via node1\",\"Verified node2<->node3 ping success through node1 (pre-restart baseline)\",\"Captured boot_id/uptime baseline on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node1 via `reboot`, polled until it returned\",\"Confirmed node1's boot_id changed, confirming a real restart\",\"Re-verified eth1/eth2 addresses, forwarding sysctls, and persisted config files on node1 post-restart\",\"Re-verified node2<->node3 ping success post-restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 has a routed address on each of its two segments\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f6ce015b9bc7441b\"],\"summary\":\"eth1 assigned 172.20.1.1/24 and eth2 assigned 172.20.2.1/24 on node1, confirmed by ip addr output\"},{\"requirement\":\"working path between node2 and node3 (pre-restart)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c763a597edf546ea\",\"cmd-a8d7c3e7cca04443\",\"cmd-31e0eed0083142c7\",\"cmd-7b18399faf964048\"],\"summary\":\"node2 (172.20.1.2/24) and node3 (172.20.2.2/24) configured with routes via node1; ping between them succeeded with 0% loss in both directions\"},{\"requirement\":\"config persisted for reboot (files written)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-31448b3fcc44400c\"],\"summary\":\"Wrote /etc/network/interfaces.d/60-antrieb-segments (static eth1/eth2 addresses, auto-sourced by SONiC's networking service) and /etc/sysctl.d/99-antrieb.conf (forwarding sysctls, applied at boot)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2046ee56d86f44c8\"],\"summary\":\"Captured node1 boot_id e5168e03-df6d-4e9f-b014-5de4bdfa0688, uptime, eth1/eth2 addresses, and ip_forward=1 before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ff7ce91380d440a3\"],\"summary\":\"Issued backgrounded `reboot` on node1; command acknowledged before the connection dropped\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 boot identity changed (proof of restart)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-74ac477b53b244a1\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart boot_id read as 5efc5171-0791-4033-b821-2efe1d991a3a, differing from the pre-restart baseline e5168e03-df6d-4e9f-b014-5de4bdfa0688, with a fresh uptime timestamp\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart recovery of required config\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1dcad3fabc9e48dc\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, eth1/eth2 addresses (172.20.1.1/24, 172.20.2.1